  {
   "id": 7985436819533,
   "title": "Finca La Hermosa - Orange Bourbon Variety",
   "handle": "finca-la-hermosa-pink-bourbon-variety-copy",
   "body_html": "<p>Finca La Hermosa is a long-dreamed-of farm with humble beginnings. In 2010, knowing the potential of Acatenango's volcanic soil, Claudia Abril and Max Perez began transforming an abandoned parcel with no electricity or water into a thriving business. Today, this land produces Cup of Excellence-winning coffees and boasts a small poultry farm and a quality lab as well.\u00a0</p>\n<p>Among the fields of traditional organic coffee, there is a trial plot of over 30 rarer varieties, such as Pacamara and Orange Bourbon. Orange Bourbon is a color mutation of the classic Bourbon variety, producing orange-ripening cherries instead of the typical red. What we love about this cup is the subtle brightness of dark stone fruits like cherry and plum, rounded out by a creamy milk-chocolate sweetness.<br></p>\n<p>Pronunciation: FEENG-kah lah ehr-MOH-sah</p>",
   "published_at": "2026-09-24T16:09:48-04:00",
   "created_at": "2026-09-17T12:27:52-04:00",
