  {
   "id": 7942307840077,
   "title": "Finca La Hermosa - Pacamara Variety",
   "handle": "finca-la-hermosa-pacamara-variety-copy",
   "body_html": "<p>Finca La Hermosa began in 2010 as an abandoned parcel on the slopes of the Acatenango volcano, with no water or electricity. Today it's a thriving family farm run by Claudia and Max, whose resourcefulness and dedication to sustainability and quality have earned them multiple Cup of Excellence placements.\u00a0</p>\n<p>Planted alongside the larger lots that go into our year-round products like Fast Forward are 32 varieties not often seen in Guatemala. Among those is Pacamara, a cross of Pacas and Maragogipe developed in El Salvador, where it dominates the national Cup of Excellence. Grown in Acatenango's volcanic soil, the variety shows similar brilliance here: complex notes of ripe honeydew and bright green apple, carried by a creamy body that ties the cup together.<br></p>\n<p>Pronunciation: FEENG-kah lah ehr-MOH-sah</p>",
   "published_at": "2026-08-27T15:58:34-04:00",
